

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                                AGESILAO







          Fabrizio Zordan
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) notified Agesilao that our friendship has 
been rendered meaningless by Agesilao's outrageous provocations.

  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Agesilao treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with 
his ally Giovanna (#7).
  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and Agesilao made ready to carry out his 
imperial assignments.  He girded his weapon and entered the Monastery 
warily.  He wielded his Holy Sword.  He encountered the Renegade Illusionist.
Agesilao thought to cast a Hand Of Death spell, but couldn't find a crucial 
material component before Agesilao could make his spellcast.  Chanting his 
silver words of magic into a mighty Hand Of Death spell, 
the Renegade Illusionist gestured with his arms and began making squeezing 
motions with his hands.
  Agesilao loped along steadily and closed to bow range.  
The Renegade Illusionist brought his hands together and pulled them apart in 
a tearing gesture, provoking a terrible squeal of pain from Agesilao and 
damaged him, inflicting 2 damage points.
  Agesilao rushed lustily into melee combat.  The Renegade Illusionist 
curled his phantasmal hand around Agesilao's heart and squeezed it and 
scorched Agesilao with 2 damage points.  With amazing speed, Agesilao 
immediately thrust at the Renegade Illusionist but his aim was just off.  
The Renegade Illusionist clenched his fist, squeezing the innards of 
Agesilao and inflicted 2 damage points.
  Agesilao feigned panic, then pivoted and swang at the Renegade Illusionist 
and inflicted 8 damage points.  The Renegade Illusionist's spell was 
disrupted by the event.  The Renegade Illusionist swang at his nemesis and 
scored 1 damage points on Agesilao.  Agesilao swang at 
the Renegade Illusionist and scorched the Renegade Illusionist with 10 
damage points.  The Renegade Illusionist dropped to the ground, mortally 
pierced.  Agesilao looked down with satisfaction at the remains of 
the Renegade Illusionist.  Agesilao secured the Large Hoard of Gold.  
Agesilao looted 23 gold from the treasure of the Renegade Illusionist.
  While scouting the Monastery, Agesilao saw a Slot Machine which seemed to 
be of a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Slot Machine, saying "The effects of the Slot 
Machine are both good and bad!  Chance will determine the fate of Agesilao, 
good or ill.  Care to take a chance?  By the power of the Slot Machine, I 
increase your skill in Thievery by 1 skill level!"
  With the coming of the early summer season Agesilao travelled to Mare 
Frigidis.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of the Argyre Sea,
a Forest area ruled by Agesilao.  The Argyre Sea was overrun and occupied by 
Hope (#94)'s host.  Hope leads approximately 2 Garrison, 1 Phalanx and 4 
Warg Riders.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Agesilao cast a 
Skeletal Army spell and no skeletons answered the spell's call.
  Apurimac was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Apurimac.
  With the advent of the fall season, Agesilao rode into the Argyre Sea.
  In early winter, Agesilao cast a Bless spell.  The Argyre Sea was 
magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in the Argyre 
Sea.


  An army sent by the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
entered Bizerte, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Agesilao and 
made up of great Forests.  Hope (#94)'s forces took Bizerte without any 
major engagements.  Hope leads approximately 2 Phalanx and 2 Warg Riders.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally II Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Agesilao 
treated with his ally Circe (#8).

  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 19 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  2 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left 
with 92 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Moosu, Squire to Tancred
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring.  Tancred travelled to Silvania.  Northwest of 
here lies the province of Jutland (#1307), ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is known to be a Mountain province 
occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish fighters prefer to array themselves in the 
style of Bowmen.  Tancred saw no monsters.
  Adonis (#69) encountered Tancred.  Adonis chanted his strange words of 
magic and cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with 
his hands.  Tancred stuck his tail between his legs and fled from Adonis as 
fast as his legs could carry Tancred!
  During early summer, Tancred rode into the Stonegard Sea.  Northwest of 
here is the Ark Royal Sea (#1306), a poor Mountain province ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll, where Orcs dwell.  Their Orcish warriors 
array themselves in the style of Legion and Warg Riders.  In his travels, 
Tancred saw no monster.
  Adonis encountered Tancred.  Lifting his hands high in the air, Adonis 
cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with his 
hands.  Tancred stuck his tail between his legs and fled from Adonis as fast 
as his legs could carry Tancred!
  In late summer, Tancred moved into the Plesiosaurus Sea.  Viewing the 
northeastern horizon, one can see a prosperous Sea province known as the 
Kilkenny Sea (#1505).  It is said that Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
reigns there.  It is known to be populated by Mermen.  They can muster an 
army of Mermen to defend their province.  Northwest of here lies the 
province of Oceanus Cyclopia (#1405), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is said to be a Sea province 
occupied by no races.  In his travels, Tancred saw no monster.
  Adonis encountered Tancred.  Lifting his hands high in the air, Adonis 
cast a Hand Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with his 
hands.  Deciding that discretion is sometimes the better part of valor, 
Tancred fled unceremoniously from the dangerous combat.
  In fall, Tancred journeyed to the Kilkenny Sea.  Turning to the northeast, 
one can see a Plain area, which is known as Milo's Crossroads (#1504).  It 
is populated by Orcs and II Kahn rules there.  Their Orcish warriors fight 
in the style of Phalanx and Heavy Cavalry.  East of here is the Vodka Sea 
(#1605), a prosperous Sea province owned by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango,
where no races dwell.  To the northwest there lies a Sea province known as 
Mammoth (#1404), an area of no races where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
rules.  In his travels, Tancred encountered no monster.
  Adonis encountered Tancred.  Casting a Hand Of Death spell, Adonis 
channelled scintillating, writhing strands of magic and began making 
squeezing motions with his hands.  Tancred tried to flee from the fight, but 
Adonis cornered Tancred.  Adonis clenched his fist, squeezing the innards of 
Tancred and inflicted 3 damage points.
  Tancred moved into bow range.  Adonis wrapped his phantasmal hand around 
Tancred's liver and squeezed it and scored on Tancred, doing 3 points of 
damage.
  Tancred charged into melee range.  He then swang at Adonis with terrific 
strength and scorched him with 2 damage points.  His spell was disrupted by 
the event.  Adonis summoned all his will and bravely swang at his fearsome 
nemesis and would have hit Tancred if Tancred hadn't ducked just then.  
Adonis immediately thrust at Tancred and scored 2 damage points on him.  
Tancred assailed Adonis but his aim was just off the mark.
  Adonis swang at Tancred and damaged him, inflicting 2 damage points.  
Hoping to take advantage of a weak point in Adonis's defenses, Tancred 
deftly thrust at Adonis but his sword whiffed through the air.  Undaunted, 
Adonis moved closer and swang at Tancred and inflicted 6 damage points.  
Tancred fell, fatally injured.  Thus did Tancred die, a defiant death by any 
standard.  Adonis stooped to collect the personal belongings of Tancred.  
Adonis took 1 gold from the treasure trove of Tancred.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Tancred


From: Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I rode my flying armies over to the Mirkwood Sea.  To the south is a 
forbidding mass of glaciers which has no end.

  Agesilao's minions initiated a campaign of conquest directed at the 
Mirkwood Sea, a Sea province owing its allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0).  I commanded the invading fleet.  The 
defenders were led by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies were 
drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Mirkwood Sea (0109):

 301st/A  
  Eagles  
 ооо09ооо 
----------
 ооо00ооо 
 103rd/A  
  Eagles  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with my ships was I.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of Babba Sissoko.
  No luck of any noteworthy significance appeared to influence the overall 
result of the engagement before it commenced.  Naval superiority was 
guaranteed by Negumba's unmatched tactical genius.
  I was frustrated by the Eagles, who virtually ignored my commands.
  Across the whole front, the 301st Eagles were arrayed against the 103rd 
Eagles.  The 301st Eagles soared over the 103rd Eagles and attacked them.  
The 103rd Eagles swooped down on the 301st Eagles and attacked without 
mercy.  The 301st Eagles fought with the 103rd Eagles and were sliced and 
diced like a blade cutting through butter.
  The acting commander's squadrons vanquished the fleet opposing them with a 
final sally.  The 103rd Eagles demolished the 301st Eagles.
  The attacking Kingdom was defeated in its attempt to take the Mirkwood Sea.
My forces completely dispersed, I escaped alone to Black Forest.
  The wet spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  I attempted an 
illegal move.  I tried to move from Black Forest to Donegal, a non-adjacent 
province.  Instead, I moved into the Mirkwood Sea.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  I rode into Katmai.  
I was told by some sheepherders of a perilous feature in Katmai, a Glade 
(#26) inhabited by the Treant.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The 
Treant is a large tree capable of moving its limbs and arms much as a man 
does.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  I could not recruit Bowmen in 
Katmai because Agesilao does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't 
available.  So, I discovered nothing worthy of note in my sagely 
experiments.
  During early winter, I travelled to Jadegate.

  Thy humble servant,   Negumba


